    {
      "id": 1,
      "url": "https://maramasaeva.com/observatory",
      "title": "Murmuration — measurements",
      "accessed": "2026-10-03",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "Every scoring rule is written down and git-committed, with a timestamp, **before** any data is scored; the commit hash is the proof it was frozen.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Across 7 records with a frozen rule (committed before any day-list existed), the most any day reaches is **K = 2**.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "We have **not found a new swarm**.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Each rule was committed before scoring and measured against ordinary-day controls. Two records carry a swarm; the rest are nulls.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "The unchanged rule reproduces the three days exactly (28 May 0.65 swarm-style / 0.16 tester-style; 6 Jul 0.93 / 0.03; 29 Sep 0.83 / 0.09).",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "29 Sep has 23 unique URLs, 17 unique digests, 17 of 23 between 20:00 and 21:59 UTC, all status 200.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "One burst passes all four conditions: a `serp-*` family, 29 Sep 2026, 33 packages, 97% single-use, 100% machine-named, create-once.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "On 29 Sep: 19 distinct HF owners each created >= 20 models (above the ~14/day September average, though within the background); the Wayback httpbin index shows a swarm-like day (5.31); and PyPI has its one rule-passing burst, the serp-* cluster (5.37).",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "url": "https://maramasaeva.com/observatory/info",
      "title": "Murmuration — information and methods",
      "accessed": "2026-10-03",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "A finding is a measurement that matches independently reported events and that a second method reproduces.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "A scanner report records the request and when it was made, not what program sent it, and the harness hosts also have ordinary users.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Submitter addresses are replaced by a short code on reading, using a random key that is destroyed after each run.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        },
        {
          "text": "The pages show counts only: no report contents, links, names or addresses.",
          "added": "2026-10-03"
        }
      ]
    },
